    <briefdescription>
<para>Strict-weak-order comparator on <computeroutput><ref refid="class_module_monom" kindref="compound">ModuleMonom</ref></computeroutput>, used by <computeroutput><ref refid="class_ints_set_a5cd9bf01c6f5dc112d8391f235bd7857_1a5cd9bf01c6f5dc112d8391f235bd7857" kindref="member">IntsSet::sort</ref></computeroutput> to reorder the insertion-ordered <computeroutput>mElements</computeroutput> list. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Defers to <computeroutput><ref refid="class_module_monom_a98f193e3093cc4e3d9bd1386183c2efd_1a98f193e3093cc4e3d9bd1386183c2efd" kindref="member">ModuleMonom::compare</ref></computeroutput> and treats anything <computeroutput>&lt;= <ref refid="submodules_2mathicgb_2src_2mathicgb_2polyring_8hpp_abaab8d42f075ee8ddc9b70951d3fd6cd_1abaab8d42f075ee8ddc9b70951d3fd6cd" kindref="member">EQ</ref></computeroutput> as &quot;less than&quot;, so equal monomials get a stable position from <computeroutput>std::sort</computeroutput>&apos;s tiebreaker rather than from this comparator. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
